-- EU: Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 (Artificial Intelligence Act), Article 50(2) and (4),
-- with the definitions they use (Art. 3(3), 3(4), 3(60)), the application date
-- (Art. 113) and the transitional period added by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744
-- (Art. 111(4)).
--
-- Source: source/eu-ai-act-2024-1689-oj.xhtml and source/eu-omnibus-2026-1744-oj.xhtml.
-- Every quotation below is copied from source/text/.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `labelling-domain`

§ `The judgements Article 50 hands to someone`

-- An evaluative standard is an input, never a computation. Each field is the
-- Regulation's own words. The Commission's Guidelines of 20.7.2026, C(2026) 5054,
-- paras 90-92, give examples on each side of the first two and say the second
-- "requires a case-specific assessment"; they are guidance, not law, and this
-- module does not apply them.
DECLARE `EU Article 50 judgements` HAS
    `the AI system performs an assistive function for standard editing`                        IS A BOOLEAN -- 50(2)
    `the AI system does not substantially alter the input data provided by the deployer or the semantics thereof` IS A BOOLEAN -- 50(2)
    `the content would falsely appear to a person to be authentic or truthful`                 IS A BOOLEAN -- 3(60)
    `the content forms part of an evidently artistic, creative, satirical, fictional or analogous work or programme` IS A BOOLEAN -- 50(4)

§ `Art. 113 and Art. 111(4) -- when Article 50 applies`

-- Art. 113: "It shall apply from 2 August 2026." None of the exceptions in points
-- (a)-(c) reaches Article 50.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Regulation applies to Article 50 on` d IF
    d AT LEAST (YMD 2026 8 2)

-- Art. 111(4), added by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744, Art. 1(39)(b):
-- "Providers of AI systems, including general-purpose AI systems, generating
-- synthetic audio, image, video or text content, that have been placed on the
-- market before 2 August 2026 shall take the necessary steps in order to comply
-- with Article 50(2) by 2 December 2026."
-- Read as: for such a provider, compliance with 50(2) is not owed before
-- 2 December 2026. NOTES fork F1.
GIVEN d IS A DATE, provider IS A `the provider of the AI system`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `compliance with Article 50(2) is owed on` d `by` provider IF
        `the Regulation applies to Article 50 on` d
    AND (    NOT provider's `its system was placed on the EU market before 2 August 2026`
         OR  d AT LEAST (YMD 2026 12 2))

§ `Art. 3 -- definitions`

-- 3(60): "'deep fake' means AI-generated or manipulated image, audio or video
-- content that resembles existing persons, objects, places, entities or events
-- and would falsely appear to a person to be authentic or truthful"
GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`, publication IS A `the publication`, judged IS AN `EU Article 50 judgements`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the content is a deep fake` content publication judged IF
        `it is AI-generated or manipulated` content
    AND `it contains image, audio or video` content
    AND publication's `the content resembles existing persons, objects, places, entities or events`
    AND judged's `the content would falsely appear to a person to be authentic or truthful`

-- 3(4): "'deployer' means a natural or legal person ... using an AI system under its
-- authority except where the AI system is used in the course of a personal
-- non-professional activity"
GIVEN publication IS A `the publication`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the publisher is a deployer` publication IF
    NOT publication's `the deployer uses the AI system in the course of a personal non-professional activity`

-- Helpers over the content's facts. "AI-generated or manipulated": the content was
-- generated by an AI system, or an AI system altered it.
GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is AI-generated or manipulated` content IF
        content's `how it came to exist` EQUALS `generated by an AI system`
    OR  NOT null (content's `the alterations an AI system made to it`)

GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it contains image, audio or video` content IF
        elem `image` (content's `the kinds it contains`)
    OR  elem `audio` (content's `the kinds it contains`)
    OR  elem `video` (content's `the kinds it contains`)

GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it contains text` content IF
        elem `free-form text` (content's `the kinds it contains`)
    OR  elem `containerised text` (content's `the kinds it contains`)

§ `Art. 50(2) -- providers must ensure outputs are marked`

-- 50(2), first sentence: "Providers of AI systems, including general-purpose AI
-- systems, generating synthetic audio, image, video or text content, shall ensure
-- that the outputs of the AI system are marked in a machine-readable format and
-- detectable as artificially generated or manipulated."
-- Third sentence: "This obligation shall not apply to the extent the AI systems
-- perform an assistive function for standard editing or do not substantially alter
-- the input data provided by the deployer or the semantics thereof, or where
-- authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences."
@ref Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, Art. 50(2), Art. 111(4), Art. 113
GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`, provider IS A `the provider of the AI system`, judged IS AN `EU Article 50 judgements`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Article 50(2) requires the provider to ensure the output is marked` content provider judged d IF
        `compliance with Article 50(2) is owed on` d `by` provider
    AND `it is AI-generated or manipulated` content
    AND NOT judged's `the AI system performs an assistive function for standard editing`
    AND NOT judged's `the AI system does not substantially alter the input data provided by the deployer or the semantics thereof`
    AND NOT provider's `the use is authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences`

-- 50(2), second sentence: the solution must be "effective, interoperable, robust and
-- reliable as far as this is technically feasible ... as may be reflected in
-- relevant technical standards". Whether a given marking meets that is not
-- computed here. Article 50(7), as replaced by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744, has the
-- Commission assess whether adherence to a code of practice "is adequate to ensure
-- compliance"; the Code's Measure 1.1 is encoded in eu-code-of-practice.l4.

§ `Art. 50(4) -- deployers must disclose deep fakes and public-interest text`

DECLARE `what Article 50(4) requires` IS ONE OF
    `no disclosure under Article 50(4)`
    `disclosure that the content has been artificially generated or manipulated`
    `disclosure of the existence of such generated or manipulated content, in a manner that does not hamper the display or enjoyment of the work`

-- 50(4), first subparagraph: "Deployers of an AI system that generates or
-- manipulates image, audio or video content constituting a deep fake, shall
-- disclose that the content has been artificially generated or manipulated. This
-- obligation shall not apply where the use is authorised by law to detect, prevent,
-- investigate or prosecute criminal offence. Where the content forms part of an
-- evidently artistic, creative, satirical, fictional or analogous work or
-- programme, the transparency obligations set out in this paragraph are limited to
-- disclosure of the existence of such generated or manipulated content in an
-- appropriate manner that does not hamper the display or enjoyment of the work."
@ref Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, Art. 50(4) first subparagraph, Art. 3(4), Art. 3(60), Art. 113
GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`, publication IS A `the publication`, judged IS AN `EU Article 50 judgements`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `what Article 50(4) requires`
`Article 50(4) on a deep fake` content publication judged d MEANS
    IF      `the Regulation applies to Article 50 on` d
        AND `the publisher is a deployer` publication
        AND `the content is a deep fake` content publication judged
        AND NOT publication's `the use is authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences`
    THEN IF   judged's `the content forms part of an evidently artistic, creative, satirical, fictional or analogous work or programme`
         THEN `disclosure of the existence of such generated or manipulated content, in a manner that does not hamper the display or enjoyment of the work`
         ELSE `disclosure that the content has been artificially generated or manipulated`
    ELSE `no disclosure under Article 50(4)`

-- 50(4), second subparagraph: "Deployers of an AI system that generates or
-- manipulates text which is published with the purpose of informing the public on
-- matters of public interest shall disclose that the text has been artificially
-- generated or manipulated. This obligation shall not apply where the use is
-- authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences
-- or where the AI-generated content has undergone a process of human review or
-- editorial control and where a natural or legal person holds editorial
-- responsibility for the publication of the content."
-- The artistic limb in the first subparagraph says "the transparency obligations
-- set out in this paragraph", which could reach text too. NOTES fork F2.
@ref Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, Art. 50(4) second subparagraph, Art. 3(4), Art. 113
GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`, publication IS A `the publication`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `what Article 50(4) requires`
`Article 50(4) on public-interest text` content publication d MEANS
    IF      `the Regulation applies to Article 50 on` d
        AND `the publisher is a deployer` publication
        AND `it contains text` content
        AND `it is AI-generated or manipulated` content
        AND publication's `the text is published with the purpose of informing the public on matters of public interest`
        AND NOT publication's `the use is authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences`
        AND NOT (    publication's `the text has undergone a process of human review or editorial control`
                 AND publication's `a natural or legal person holds editorial responsibility for the publication`)
    THEN `disclosure that the content has been artificially generated or manipulated`
    ELSE `no disclosure under Article 50(4)`
